      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nWith `--disable-hybrid-kv-cache-manager`, KV cache planning crashes on any model with `SlidingWindowMLASpec` layers (DeepSeek-V4), because promotion to `MLAAttentionSpec` forwards the SWA-only `bounded_replay` field. Introduced by the interaction of #56227 (adds `bounded_replay`) and #61183 (moves the promotion into `kv_cache_planning.py`).\n\n## Claims\n\n- Fixes `TypeError: MLAAttentionSpec.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'bounded_replay'` at startup for sliding-window MLA models with the hybrid KV cache manager disabled.\n- Adds a regression test for `unify_hybrid_kv_cache_specs` with a `SlidingWindowMLASpec` layer, which no existing test covered.\n\n## Validation\n\n**Unit test**, run on MI300X (gfx942) in a ROCm 7.2 image built from this branch's tree; the fix was reverse-applied to the installed package for the \"without\" column:\n\n| | `-k swa_mla` | full `tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_planning.py` |\n|---|---|---|\n| without fix | 1 failed (the `TypeError` above) | 62 passed, 1 failed (the new test) |\n| with fix | 1 passed | 63 passed |\n\n```bash\npytest tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_planning.py -k swa_mla\n```\n\n**End to end**, DeepSeek-V4-Flash and DeepSeek-V4-Pro, disaggregated prefill/decode (MoRIIO connector, 2P/2D and 4P/4D, `-tp 1` + DP + EP), MI300X, `--disable-hybrid-kv-cache-manager`:\n\n- without the fix, every worker dies in `_promote_local_kv_cache_specs` during `get_kv_cache_configs`;\n- with the fix, all prefill and decode workers start, size their KV cache, and serve requests (concurrency sweeps 1–32 at 1024/1024 complete on both models).\n\n```bash\nvllm serve deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash --disable-hybrid-kv-cache-manager ...\n```\n\n## Details\n\nWhen the hybrid KV cache manager is off and full-attention layers are present, `_promote_local_kv_cache_specs` rebuilds each sliding-window spec as its full-attention counterpart through `replace_as`, which forwards every field of the source spec. `SlidingWindowMLASpec` has two fields `MLAAttentionSpec` lacks: `extra_retained_tokens`, which was already dropped, and `bounded_replay`, which was not. The field is always present, so the crash happens even at its default `False`.\n\nDropping it is semantically right for the same reason as `extra_retained_tokens`: a promoted spec allocates blocks for every token and never frees below the window, so window-bounded prefix replay has nothing to bound. The promoted spec reports the ordinary full-attention `prefix_cacheable`, which is correct because it retains the full prefix.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
